    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0302" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.893/2–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        President Truman</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-24">24 February 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[244.] <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: The Generalissimo
                    returned from a 10-day trip this afternoon, Sunday, stopping at his country
                    place. He asks me to motor down to talk to him and dine with him tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile, I am informed that he has approved our agreement for demobilization,
                    reorganization, and integration of the Chinese armies. The meeting to sign the
                    agreement by my committee is set for 4:00 PM tomorrow. A complete press release
                    will probably follow shortly, I suppose.</p>
                <p>Executive Headquarters in Peiping is charged with the execution of the agreement.
                    I will radio full details later.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
